DESCRIPTION >
    - What a stars request reads, as one row: the GitHub repositories in scope and the segments in scope that can hold GitLab `star` activities. Shared by `stars_github_as_of.pipe`, `stars_count.pipe` and `stars_cumulative_count.pipe`.
    - Callers read it as the scalar subquery `(SELECT scope FROM stars_scope)`. ClickHouse computes an identical scalar subquery once per query, so the dimension tables are scanned once per request, and a size check on either list is a constant that skips whole reads.
    - GitHub repositories: enabled, not excluded, hosted on github.com, plus the optional `repos` filter. Same project and collection scoping as `activities_filtered.pipe`.
    - GitLab segments: segments of GitLab integrations, and of repositories hosted on GitLab or synced by a GitLab integration. Deleted integrations and repositories are included, since their activities stay in place. An activity takes the segment its repository is mapped to, which can differ from its integration's segment, so both lists are needed. GitLab is the only integration that still emits `star` activities.
    - Parameters: `project` or `collectionSlug` with `bucketId`, `repos`, as passed to the calling pipe.
    - Response: one row with `scope`, a tuple of `githubRepositoryIds` and `gitlabSegmentIds`.

NODE stars_scope_github_repositories
SQL >
    %
    {% if defined(collectionSlug) %}
        SELECT r.id AS repositoryId
        FROM repositories r FINAL
        WHERE
            {% if defined(bucketId) %}
                isNull (r.deletedAt)
                AND r.enabled = true
                AND r.excluded = false
                AND r.url LIKE 'https://github.com/%'
                AND r.segmentId IN (SELECT segmentId FROM segments_filtered_by_collection)
                {% if defined(repos) %}
                    AND has(
                        arrayMap(
                            x -> lower(x),
                            {{ Array(repos, 'String', description="Repository URLs", required=False) }}
                        ),
                        lower(r.url)
                    )
                {% end %}
            {% else %} 1 = 0
            {% end %}
    {% else %}
        SELECT r.id AS repositoryId
        FROM repositories r FINAL
        INNER JOIN insightsProjects i FINAL ON r.insightsProjectId = i.id
        WHERE
            isNull (r.deletedAt)
            AND r.enabled = true
            AND r.excluded = false
            AND r.url LIKE 'https://github.com/%'
            AND isNull (i.deletedAt)
            AND i.enabled = 1
            AND r.segmentId = (SELECT segmentId FROM segments_filtered)
            {% if defined(repos) %}
                AND has(
                    arrayMap(
                        x -> lower(x),
                        {{ Array(repos, 'String', description="Repository URLs", required=False) }}
                    ),
                    lower(r.url)
                )
            {% end %}
    {% end %}

NODE stars_scope_gitlab_segments
SQL >
    %
    SELECT DISTINCT segmentId
    FROM
        (
            SELECT segmentId
            FROM integrations FINAL
            WHERE platform = 'gitlab'
            UNION ALL
            SELECT r.segmentId AS segmentId
            FROM repositories r FINAL
            LEFT JOIN integrations i FINAL ON r.sourceIntegrationId = i.id
            WHERE i.platform = 'gitlab' OR domain(r.url) LIKE '%gitlab%'
        )
    WHERE
        {% if defined(collectionSlug) %}
            segmentId IN (SELECT segmentId FROM segments_filtered_by_collection)
        {% else %} segmentId = (SELECT segmentId FROM segments_filtered)
        {% end %}

NODE stars_scope_row
SQL >
    SELECT
        CAST(
            (g.ids, l.ids), 'Tuple(githubRepositoryIds Array(String), gitlabSegmentIds Array(String))'
        ) AS scope
    FROM (SELECT groupArray(repositoryId) AS ids FROM stars_scope_github_repositories) g
    CROSS JOIN (SELECT groupArray(segmentId) AS ids FROM stars_scope_gitlab_segments) l
